course: dictionary
lesson: 15956
title: Untangle: undoing knots and muddles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Untangle is a verb. It means to undo knots or twists, or to make a muddle clear. The word «tangle» is hiding inside it, and «un-» at the front means undo, so untangle means to undo a tangle.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Sam sat on his bed and untangled his headphones.» Headphones are things that can get knotted, so untangled must mean he undid the knots. Swap in the meaning: "Sam sat on his bed and undid the knots in his headphones" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: You can also untangle a problem or a story. «Priya read the puzzle again and untangled the steps one by one.» A puzzle cannot be knotted like wool, but its parts can be muddled, and untangling them means sorting them out until they are clear.
fact: Untangle means to undo knots or twists.
fact: To untangle a problem or story means to make it clear, step by step.
fact: Untangle is a verb: untangle, untangles, untangled, untangling.
fact: The word «tangle» means a knot or a muddle, and «un-» at the start means undo.
fact: «Untangled» means undid the knots or made something clear.
exercise: «Dad untangled the Christmas lights before we put them up.» What does untangled mean here? | Broke them into pieces | Threw them away | Painted them | *Undid the knots
exercise: «Ella untangled the tricky maths problem step by step.» What does untangled mean here? | Wrote a story about it | *Made the problem clear by working through it | Made the problem harder | Ignored the problem
exercise: «The fishing line was knotted and messy, so Tom slowly untangled it.» Find and copy the word that describes the line before Tom untangles it. | *knotted | slowly | fishing | Tom
test: «Mum spent ten minutes untangling her hair after the windy walk.» What is Mum doing? | *Undoing the knots in her hair | Brushing her teeth | Drying it with a towel | Cutting her hair off
test: What does a teacher help you do when she helps you untangle a muddled story? | Write it in capital letters | *Make it clear | Make it longer | Hide the ending
exam: «The detective untangled the lies and found the thief.» What does untangled most likely mean here? | *Made the muddle clear and found the truth | Forgot all the lies | Told even more lies | Tied the lies into a bigger knot
